pokeplatinum-widepointers8.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies it to build/pokeplatinum, after widepointers7.patch): the movement
offset of ApplyMovement is a signed distance from the script pointer (a label before the command is a negative one: Route 201's
rival-follows scene, whose movement lists sit above its script). pret reads it as u32, which on the DS wraps modulo 2^32 to the
right address; on a 64-bit host `scriptPtr + u32` added 4 GiB and the movement task read unmapped memory (SIGSEGV in
MovementAnimation_Set). The jump commands already read s32; this one reads s32 too.
diff --git a/src/scrcmd.c b/src/scrcmd.c
--- a/src/scrcmd.c
+++ b/src/scrcmd.c
@@ -2039,5 +2039,5 @@
 {
     u16 localID = ScriptContext_GetVar(ctx);
-    u32 movementOffset = ScriptContext_ReadWord(ctx);
+    s32 movementOffset = (s32)ScriptContext_ReadWord(ctx);
     MapObject *object = GetLocalMapObjByIndex(ctx->fieldSystem, localID);
     if (object == NULL) {
